From 390774294e07ba42743d426ece2c0b4a17733247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:36:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 293/346] Assembly: a big step of a driving value walks there
 instead of dropping the driver

Driving a joint by a big step (a crank from 0 to 90 degrees) did not
converge: the solver dropped the driving joint as redundant, solve()
returned 0 and the parts did not move (engine field test 0.6.9). After a
solve the joints that pin parts together (fixed, revolute, ball) are
checked; if they do not hold, the joints' placements are walked from the
last solve that held to the asked ones in steps of at most 15 degrees.
If they still do not hold, solve() returns -7 with a warning.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
